  "decisionRules": [
    "EXPLICIT_RECORD_OR_SESSION_TIME outranks provider publication time when the source states what the time means.",
    "A documented range is preserved as the canonical date text and sorts from the range start.",
    "A core event date may drive chronology when the page is itself a record of that event and no stronger record timestamp conflicts.",
    "A date merely mentioned as subject matter, external history, schema example, or child-record index entry does not establish the page date.",
    "MULTI_EVENT_RECORD without one explicit record/session date remains held rather than choosing the first or last mentioned event.",
    "SQUARESPACE_DATE_PUBLISHED is fallback provenance only when an exact wrapper survives and no stronger authored record time exists; dateModified never becomes record time by default.",
    "Chronology admission does not preassign node id; application allocates identity against exact current main.",
    "Timeline admission may expose a not-yet-live/WIP record as missing rather than hiding known chronology."
  ],
